No — the log pattern (idle=0, waiting climbing steadily and monotonically, never recovering) is a leak signature, not a capacity one. If pool size were just too small, idle would fluctuate as clients cycle through; here nothing is ever returned.

The cause is in db.js:11-16 — `withClient` calls `client.release()` only after `fn(client)` succeeds. If `fn` throws, the client is never released and stays checked out forever, so the pool permanently shrinks toward 0 available connections. Raising `max` would just delay the same climb.

