The bug is in db.js:11-16: `withClient` calls `client.release()` only after `fn(client)` resolves. If `fn` throws, the client is never released and stays checked out forever. Each failing call permanently shrinks the effective pool until all 20 are stuck, which lines up with the log.

Fix:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

