If `fn(client)` throws, `client.release()` is never reached, so that connection is permanently held. Each failing call leaks one connection until the pool is exhausted — which matches `idle` staying at 0 while `waiting` grows unbounded. Wrap the release in `finally`:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

