The cause is in `db.js:11-16`: `withClient` calls `client.release()` only after `fn(client)` resolves. If `fn` throws, `release()` is skipped and that client is leaked forever. Under load, errors accumulate and the pool drains to zero idle connections while requests pile up in the wait queue — exactly what the log shows.

