```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

Raising `max` would only delay the exhaustion, not stop it — leaked clients still accumulate and you'd hit a new, higher ceiling later.

